  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I couldn't find an earlier ticket reporting this same problem: typing a drive path such as c:\\\\ or c:/ into Command Palette and pinning it to the Dock does nothing, while a manually mapped drive works. The closest ticket, PowerToys#46254, is about pinning a folder from a fallback search result to the Dock. It says fallback items depend on the exact text typed and shouldn't be pinnable. It also says pinning files and folders needs IDs added, which was planned but not confirmed as fixed. That may be related to your case, but it isn't the same report. Please keep this ticket open and add your Windows version, plus the exact steps you used to try to pin the drive (right-click, then Pin to Dock). If you can, also attach a PowerToys bug report ZIP so the team can look at the CmdPal logs. In the meantime, use the mapped drive, which you say works.\"}",
